    "guide": {
      "schemaVersion": 1,
      "installation": "When listed, search **Living Code** under publisher **living-code-theme** in the VS Code Marketplace or Open VSX, install it, then run *Preferences: Color Theme → Living Code Night*. The extension ID is `living-code-theme.living-code`.\n\n**Without a marketplace:** download `living-code-0.1.1.vsix` from the [latest GitHub release](https://github.com/living-code-theme/vscode/releases/latest), or build it from a checkout:\n\n```sh\nnode scripts/package.mjs\ncode --install-extension dist/living-code-0.1.1.vsix\n```\n\nChoose another Living Code flavor with the color-theme picker.",
      "configuration": "The extension supplies color themes, not fonts or editor settings. Keep your existing preferences. Use VS Code's `workbench.colorCustomizations` and `editor.tokenColorCustomizations` settings for personal overrides.",
      "compatibility": "Supports the `engines.vscode` compatibility range in package.json and all four Living Code themes. The same VSIX can be used in compatible VS Code forks. Marketplace updates use the extension ID `living-code-theme.living-code`; installations from another publisher do not switch automatically.",
      "links": {}
    },
